---
title: "Otium docs"
prompt: |
  Write the index page for docs/: a few sentences on what Otium, Manse and otos
  are, then a linked list of every doc with one line on each.
---

Then explain how the docs are made, from `tools/generate-docs` and
`tools/check-docs`:

- A doc with a `.md.spec` beside it is generated by Pi from that spec
  and has ✨ in its title. A doc without a spec is written by hand and has no ✨.
- What a spec contains (front matter with `title` and `prompt`, and an optional
  body), with a short example.
- The default is openai-codex/gpt-6-astra with medium reasoning and normal
  service tier. Provider and model can be overridden with --provider/--model
  or DOCS_PROVIDER/DOCS_MODEL. Pi must be installed and authenticated.
- README.md and AGENTS.md are protected and skipped by the generator.
- How to regenerate all docs or some with `just docs`, the dry-run flag, and
  that generated docs should be reviewed before committing.
- How to add a new generated doc, and how to turn a generated doc into a
  hand-written one (delete the spec, drop the ✨).

Mention `specs/` for designs and AGENT-LANG.md for agents writing Otium.
Keep it short.
